ENTRY            32580   20240216   20240400   20240331       3211
SUBENT        32580001   20240216   20240400   20240331       3211
BIB                 14         33
TITLE      Measurement of secondary neutron double differential
            cross section from 209Bi at 14.2 MeV
AUTHOR     (Shen Guanren, Xia Haihong, Tang Hongqing, Zhou Zuying,
            Sui Qingchang, Qi Bujia, Ke Zunjian, Zhou Chenwei)
INSTITUTE  (3CPRAEP)
REFERENCE  (J,CNP,14,234,1992)
           (C,91BEIJIN,,46,1991)
FACILITY   (CCW,3CPRAEP)
INC-SOURCE (D-T)
SAMPLE     Metal Bi, 3 cm in diameter, 3 cm in length
METHOD     (TOF) flight path 2.7m, resolution time 1.2 ns,
            energy resolution about 5% for 14.2 MeV neutron
           (PSD) pulse shape discriminator to reduce gamma ray,
            biased at 1.3 MeV.
DETECTOR   (SCIN) Liquid scintilator
MONITOR    (1-H-1(N,N)1-H-1,,DA)
CORRECTION Corrections were made, using the monte carlo code DCM,
           for multiple scattering,incident neutron flux
           attenuation and finite geometry.
ERR-ANALYS (ERR-T) Total uncertainty consists:
           (ERR-S,10.,20.) counting statistics          (~10-20%)
           (ERR-1)         neutron detector efficiency      (~3%)
           (ERR-2,1.5,3.)  Monte Carlo correction error (~1.5-3%)
           (MONIT-ERR)     standard cross section            (1%)
STATUS     (TABLE) Data taken from the authors
           (APRVD) proof-copy approved by authors and authors
            corrections have been entered
HISTORY    (19930416R) Data taken from the authors
           (19930416C) Compiled by Liu Tingjin, CNDC
           (19930825A) HW.-Reference and subents 009, 010
            (previous subents 31404002, 31404003) added.-
           (20090730U) SD: Updated to new date formats, lower case
           (20240216U) On. REFERENCE(CNP): Issue number deleted.
ENDBIB              33
COMMON               5          3
EN         ANG-NRM    MONIT      ERR-1      MONIT-ERR
MEV        ADEG       MB/SR      PER-CENT   PER-CENT
 14.2        25.        192.1       3.0        1.0
ENDCOMMON            3
ENDSUBENT           40
ENDENTRY             1
